Conclusion:
- LSB bitset sizing remains corrected; the old MSB-first 2026-style F1 count is not used.
- Compact witness/no-good lowering is still cheap across all families.
- Expanded/geometric lowering must be capped on the final CONCRETE literal vector
  (after group/template/optional expansion), NOT just the type-pool count.
- Current F9 certs are single-group; all-mfg/group-all numbers are stress proxies,
  not the present F9 per-cut concrete literal vector.
- type-pool UBs (F9 3341, F4 5429, ~16-18K) are cheap proxies, not real-master literal bounds.
- Budgets must remain constraint-kind-specific: linear about 4 B/term, BoolOr/no-good about 11 B/term.
- P1.3A guard: per-cut max/p99 cap + cumulative proto budget after group/template/optional resolution.
